{
  "_comment": [
    "Installed at /opt/sandbroker/etc/sandbroker.json as root:root 0444.",
    "It holds NO secrets: vault names, token FILENAMES, ports and paths only.",
    "Safe for the agent to read, and reading it is how the agent learns what",
    "vaults exist.",
    "",
    "bind: leave null for unix-socket-only, which is the default and the",
    "tightest setting. Set it to a tailnet (100.64.0.0/10) or loopback address",
    "to also expose MCP over HTTP. The daemon REFUSES any other address: the",
    "HTTP surface is unauthenticated by design, so reachability is the whole",
    "access control."
  ],

  "op_bin": "/usr/local/bin/op",
  "tokens_dir": "/opt/sandbroker/var/tokens",
  "socket_dir": "/opt/sandbroker/run",
  "alerts_dir": "/opt/sandbroker/var/alerts",
  "socket_group": "claude-broker",

  "bind": null,

  "_notify_comment": [
    "notify_command is how a leak alert reaches you, and it is whatever command",
    "you want. A string runs under /bin/sh; a list is argv and skips the shell.",
    "The alert arrives as JSON on stdin and as SANDBROKER_ALERT_* environment",
    "variables. Exit 0 means delivered; anything else is a failure the sweeper",
    "retries every 15 minutes until a human acknowledges the alert on the host.",
    "",
    "Nothing the agent wrote is ever placed in the command line, so a hostile",
    "`detail` string cannot become shell.",
    "",
    "Leave it null and alerts are still recorded to disk, but no one is told.",
    "`sandbroker doctor` reports that as a problem, because an alarm nobody",
    "hears is worse than no alarm at all.",
    "",
    "Examples:",
    "  \"notify_command\": \"/opt/sandbroker/contrib/notify-ntfy.sh\"",
    "  \"notify_command\": \"notify-send -u critical \\\"$SANDBROKER_ALERT_TITLE\\\"\"",
    "  \"notify_command\": [\"/usr/local/bin/page-me\", \"--severity\", \"high\"]",
    "  \"notify_command\": \"jq -c . >> /var/log/sandbroker-leaks.jsonl\""
  ],

  "notify_command": "/opt/sandbroker/contrib/notify-ntfy.sh",

  "max_output_bytes": 1048576,
  "default_timeout": 60,
  "max_timeout": 600,

  "_vault_comment": [
    "require_unlock gates a vault: no secret from it is resolved until a human",
    "runs `sudo sandbroker unlock <Vault>`, and the unlock expires on its own.",
    "The enforcement is the filesystem, not code -- the marker directory is 0700",
    "and owned by the broker, so writing one needs root or the broker user, and",
    "typing that sudo password IS the approval.",
    "",
    "Only `run` is gated. list_items and list_fields return names, never values,",
    "so gating them would add friction without adding safety."
  ],

  "_vault_naming_comment": [
    "The key is the ALIAS the agent sees; `vault` is the real name in 1Password.",
    "They differ on purpose: the alias survives a vault rename, and the real",
    "naming never appears in agent-visible strings. `token` is a FILENAME under",
    "tokens_dir, not a token."
  ],

  "vaults": {
    "Dev":        {"vault": "Acme - Dev",        "token": "Dev",        "port": 8770},
    "Staging":    {"vault": "Acme - Staging",    "token": "Staging",    "port": 8771},
    "Production": {"vault": "Acme - Production", "token": "Production", "port": 8772,
                   "require_unlock": true},
    "Infra":      {"vault": "Acme - Infra",      "token": "Infra",      "port": 8773,
                   "require_unlock": true}
  }
}
